---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Cookies & storage"
  description="The local preferences WizardLoop saves, how optional Telegram embeds work, and how to change or remove your choices."
>
  <section class="wrap prose-page">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">YOUR BROWSER, YOUR CHOICE</p>
      <h1>
        A few preferences.
        <br />
        No analytics.
      </h1>
      <p>
        This site does not add advertising or analytics cookies. It uses local
        browser storage for choices you make and asks before loading optional
        Telegram content.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reviewed <time datetime="2026-10-27">27 October 2026</time>.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What this website remembers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Theme:</strong> your light or dark appearance choice.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Motion:</strong> whether you paused the site's animation. Your
          system's reduced-motion setting is also respected.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Telegram preference:</strong> whether you chose to allow
          optional embedded posts.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These values use local storage, which is different from a cookie but
        still stores information in your browser. They are not used to create a
        marketing profile. They remain until you change them or clear this
        site's data. If storage is blocked, the site still works and preferences
        may not persist.
      </p>

      <h2>External services</h2>
      <p>
        Optional Telegram embeds stay unloaded until you choose to enable them.
        Telegram can then process connection information and use its own cookies
        or storage. You can leave embeds disabled and open the original post
        separately. The{' '}
        <a href="https://telegram.org/privacy">Telegram Privacy Policy</a>{' '}
        describes its practices.
      </p>
      <p>
        When the feedback form is configured, Cloudflare Turnstile provides an
        anti-abuse check. Its explanation appears before loading the check. It
        is not an analytics or advertising integration; Cloudflare still
        processes technical information needed for its service. See{' '}
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">
          Cloudflare's Privacy Policy
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <p>
        There is no blanket consent banner for features this site does not use.
        Optional external posts have their own choice at the point where you
        would load them.
      </p>

      <h2>Change your preferences</h2>
      <p>
        Use the theme and motion controls in the header to change those
        settings. Use the Telegram preference control on the Posts page to
        withdraw permission for embeds. Declining is available without
        preventing access to the rest of the site.
      </p>
      <p>
        <button class="button" type="button" data-privacy-open>
          Manage external content
        </button>
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/posts/">
          Visit the Posts page
        </a>
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also clear local storage and cookies through your browser's
        site-data settings. Clearing this site's data resets its choices.
        Telegram-owned cookies must be cleared for Telegram's domain, and
        withdrawing permission does not reverse information already sent to a
        provider.
      </p>
      <p>
        For questions, see the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> or email{' '}
        <a href="mailto:wizard@wizardloop.com">wizard@wizardloop.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
